<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/434801ATBQDKBTRQSDBLVQKCTMGMVMDSD>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Darby Mills True Story";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/49bac145-f539-4f0d-819c-7b76131ed570.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Darby Mills Project presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">DARBY MILLS TRUE STORY</span></h1></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">DARBY MILLS: TRUE STORY</span> isn't just a concert. It's a full-throttle autobiographical rock show!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Darby Mills takes her life story <span class=\"BoldText\">LIVE</span> to the stage. Her world-class band rocks the floor while 21 exclusive videos of rare footage, photos and memories from her five decades on the road light up the big screen.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>It's raw. It's real. It's funny. It's <span class=\"BoldText\">LOUD.</span> It's the story behind the voice!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>From a high school stage at 16, to club bands across Western Canada at 18, to joining the Headpins in 1980 at 20 and hitting the road across North America and Europe with ZZ Top, Whitesnake, KISS, Loverboy, Eddie Money, Quiet Riot and more, Darby tells it all. She brings the songs that got her here roaring back to life while the band kicks in on some wicked grooves.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">The Show Includes</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">ALL THE HEADPINS HITS</span><span><br/></span>\"Don't It Make Ya Feel.\" \"Just One More Time.\" \"Turn It Loud.\" \"Feel My Body.\" \"Don't You Know You're Winning.\" \"Line of Fire.\"<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>And that's just the start! Darby also plays more from her three-album run at the top of the Canadian charts, plus some European releases you never got to hear in Canada.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">THE SONGS THAT MOLDED HER</span><span><br/></span>The legendary voices and bands that fired up her sound and explosive stage presence: Led Zeppelin. Janis Joplin. The Allman Brothers. Nazareth. And a few more surprises!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About Darby Mills</span><span><br/></span>Darby burst onto the music scene a week after high school graduation in 1978. Two years later she joined the Headpins, earning 4× platinum success with <span class=\"ItalicText\">Turn It Loud</span> and becoming one of Canada's most iconic rock frontwomen. After 36 years on the road with the band, she reinvented herself in 2016 with the Darby Mills Project. When COVID shut down the arts in 2020, she spent 20-plus months learning video editing, then created and launched <span class=\"ItalicText\">TRUE STORY</span>, her live Rocumentary.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Never give up on your dreams, never look back, and don't be afraid to fly solo!</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular  $49.00</span>  ($40.25 base price + $2.36 CIF + $6.39 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices are CAD and include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mary Irwin Theatre at the Rotary Centre for the Arts event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Darby Mills True Story</span> ticket fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
