<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/431401ATHVNTLPJJDJNCNQKLCQSLQQNPH>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Jordan Jensen";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/faa3e7ae-eb40-4c20-b800-94ff9bf564d0.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>MRG Live presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">JORDAN JENSEN</span></h1><h2><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">The Wet Hug Tour</span></span></h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>Jordan Jensen is a stand-up comedian and actor whose critically acclaimed hour long comedy special, TAKE ME WITH YOU, debuted on Netflix and was praised by Decider as “a winning comedy debut that takes on femininity standards”.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Jordan is currently on tour, selling out venues and adding shows by popular demand. She has amassed nearly 2 million followers across her social media platforms and has over 2.5 million views on her YouTube special. Jordan has built a strong digital following alongside her podcasts — co-hosting “Bein’ Ian with Jordan” and hosting her own, \"RIP Jordan Jensen.\"<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Jordan can be seen in Bradley Cooper's feature IS THIS THING ON? for Searchlight starring Will Arnett and was recently a staff writer on Season 2 of Tom Segura’s Netflix series BAD THOUGHTS. In 2025, Jordan was spotlighted in Deadline's \"The Future Of Funny: 15 Comedians Ready To Break Out In 2025\", following her earlier recognition in Vulture’s “Comedians You Should and Will Know”. She has appeared on The Late Late Show with James Corden, Comedy Central Features, Don’t Tell Comedy, Vice’s Super Maximum Retro Show with Chris Distefano and voiced the lead character in Adult Swim's \"The Elephant\". In 2021, she became the first female comic to win NY’s Funniest Stand-Up Award at the New York Comedy Festival<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 1  $59.29</span>  ($49.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $7.43 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 2  $47.79</span>  ($39.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $5.93 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 3  $43.19</span>  ($35.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $5.33 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Kelowna Community Theatre event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Jordan Jensen</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
