<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/431601AVQBTQMMLPTPVNDHNVMPHBLGRVQ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Living Things Festival - CLÀSSICS by Jordi Bertran (KCT)";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/7f2bd3a7-5e7b-4fab-95dd-ac55450873ab.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Living Things Festival presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">CLÀSSICS BY JORDI BERTRAN</span></h1><h2>An Intimate On-Stage Performance</h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>Puppetry // Spain<span><br/></span>January 22, 7:30 PM at the Kelowna Community Theatre<span><br/></span>For all audiences.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Join us for a special performance by internationally acclaimed puppeteer Jordi Bertran at the Kelowna Community Theatre. Audience members will be seated on stage for an intimate, up-close experience of Bertran's remarkable artistry. Seated is limited. Following the performance, stay for an artist talk with Jordi Bertran.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Jordi Bertran is an internationally renowned puppeteer, musician, and creator known for his distinctive visual language rooted in gesture and poetic expression. His work has toured internationally, received numerous awards, and captivated audiences of all ages. He is also a dedicated educator, sharing his practice with new generations of artists.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>CLÀSSICS is a selection of Jordi Bertran's finest puppet scenes, created throughout his extensive career. This cabaret-style performance for audiences of all ages brings together characters from his previous productions, delighting audiences with humour, movement, and expressive storytelling. Bertran brings more than 45 years of artistic experience across five continents to this remarkable production. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Join us for a pre-show reception in the theatre lobby at 6:30pm.<span><br/></span>Theatre doors open at 7:20pm.<span><br/></span>Performance begins at 7:30pm.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>CLÀSSICS Video Trailer: <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://vimeo.com/1218189398/2cd92adaeb?fl=ip&amp;fe=ec&amp;share=copy\">https://vimeo.com/1218189398/2cd92adaeb?fl=ip&amp;fe=ec&amp;share=copy</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Half-priced tickets are available for students on the website or at the theatre's Box Office.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Living Things is presented by Inner Fish Performance, a Kelowna-based non-profit performing arts organization.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Supporter</span> <span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I would like to support inclusive pricing and help make lower-priced tickets available to others.</span>  <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$71.36</span>  ($60.00 base price + $2.36 CIF  + $9.00 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I would like to support arts and culture in Kelowna and am able to pay the full price of a ticket.</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$54.11</span>  ($45.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $6.75 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Student</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I am a student and would like to enjoy arts and culture at an affordable price.</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$28.24</span>  ($22.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $3.38 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Kelowna Community Theatre event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">CLÀSSICS by Jordi Bertran</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
