<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/428601ATHBBPRMCRMVJPLCQGMPVTVJQDH>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Living Things Festival - Objects in Motion";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/888d1079-5b1e-41c3-95af-e5a334f7ef0f.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Living Things Festival presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">OBJECTS IN MOTION</span></h1></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>Experimental Animated Short films // International<span><br/></span>January 26, 7:00 PM at the Mary Irwin Theatre<span><br/></span>For mature audiences<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Objects in Motion is a one-of-a-kind selection of international experimental animated short films. Curated by local artist, professor, and animator Myron Campbell, the films push the boundaries of storytelling and animation. Whether showcasing hand-drawn, stop-motion with physical materials, paper theatre, handheld and digital puppetry, Objects in Motion promises a diverse and emotionally impactful evening of films, ranging from hilarity to pointed social critique. And it’s one night only! This is a Festival Favourite!  Don’t miss the chance to experience these unique films live in the company of other living things…<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2>INCLUSIVE PRICING*<span><br/></span>In a spirit of openness and accessibility, we invite everyone to choose the ticket price that best suits their situation.<span><br/></span> <span><br/></span>Half-priced tickets are available for students on the website or at the theatre’s Box Office.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>With support from the UBCO - Faculty of Creative and Critical Studies.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Living Things is presented by Inner Fish Performance, a Kelowna-based non-profit performing arts organization.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Supporter</span> <span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I would like to support inclusive pricing and help make lower-priced tickets available to others.</span>  <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$42.96</span>  ($35.00 base price + $2.36 CIF  + $5.60 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I would like to support arts and culture in Kelowna and am able to pay the full price of a ticket.</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$31.46</span>  ($25.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $4.10 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Student</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I am a student and would like to enjoy arts and culture at an affordable price.</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$19.99</span>  ($15.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $2.63 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Reduced Rate</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">I have a limited budget for cultural activities but don't want to miss out.</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$17.49</span>  ($12.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $2.63 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mary Irwin Theatre at the Rotary Centre for the Arts event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Objects in Motion</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
