  schema:name "Opera Kelowna presents La Bohème";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/ee4b699a-3915-4c85-8128-25f2c649797e.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Opera Kelowna presents <span class=\"BoldText\">La Bohème</span></h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">How does love illuminate you?</span> </h1></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">La Bohème</span><span class=\"BoldText\"> </span>is one of the most beloved operas throughout the world, and with good reason. Puccini’s soaring melodies and rich musical textures weave the individual experiences of these young Parisians into a musical narrative that feels unforgettable, organic and incredibly rich.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Four friends (Rodolofo, Marcello, Schaunard and Colline) balance their lives between their artistic ambitions and realities of poverty without losing their good cheer. One winter’s night, a neighbourly meet-cute changes everything when Mimì meets Rodolfo and they fall instantly in love. Joined by singer Musetta, the friends and lovers celebrate everything that life has to offer them, including taking over the nearby Café Momus for a raucous evening. But it also becomes clear quickly that Mimì is ill. As the months progress, Rodolfo and Mimì struggle to preserve their love as life gets in the way. Musetta reunites with Marcello, only to confirm once more that their love is too tempestuous to last. Rodolfo, hoping Mimì might find someone who can better support her through her illness, breaks off their relationship. As spring arrives, Marcello, Rodolfo, Colline and Schaunard try to make light of their sorrow and hunger in a game of make-believe back in their garret apartment. Musetta arrives with a gravely ill Mimì, and the friends rush to pawn anything of value in order to afford her some measure of comfort in her darkest hour.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Working in the <span class=\"ItalicText\">verismo</span> tradition of crafting operas that explore everyday people and the lives they live, Puccini and his librettists include the orchestra as a character throughout the work. Famous arias such as Rodolfo’s “Che gelida manina” (“What a cold little hand”) and Musetta’s “Quando m’en vo” (“When I go along”) move the story forward and also offer audiences an intimate look at the characters who sing them. Because the opera is through-composed, meaning it doesn’t stop between musical numbers, these “showstoppers” are intertwined with other music so that the story moves constantly, like a flowing river.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Opera Kelowna's original production:</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Director Glynis Leyshon sets this production traditionally, in mid-1800s Paris, against a backdrop of café culture, bustling urban life, and social revolution always around the corner. The production explores lives lived with joy, artistry and meaning – even when precarity, poverty and illness cast ever bigger shadows. It is performed by an all-Canadian cast, with live orchestra, and sung in Italian with English subtitles provided.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>For cast and additional information visit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.operakelowna.com/production/la-boheme/\">operakelowna.com</a> <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span>Adult:<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 1: $105.00</span> ($89.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $13.39 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 2: $92.06</span> ($78.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $11.70 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 3: $79.41</span> ($67.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $10.05 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Senior (65+):<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 1: $92.68</span> ($78.54 base price + $2.36 CIF + $11.78 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 2: $81.30</span> ($68.64 base price + $2.36 CIF + $10.30 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 3: $70.16</span> ($58.96 base price + $2.36 CIF + $8.84 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Student (under 18):<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 1: $100.98</span> ($87.24 base price + $2.36 CIF + $11.38 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 2: $78.61</span> ($66.30 base price + $2.36 CIF + $9.95 Service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 3: $67.85</span> ($56.95 base price + $2.36 CIF + $8.54 Service Fee)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">*Limited Pay-What-You-Wish tickets available.</span><span><br/></span><ul><li> Pay-What-You-Wish tickets are available ranging from $5.00 - $25.00 in increments of $5.00. </li><li> $2.36 CIF and $1.05 + 5% Service Fee are added to each Pay-What-You-Wish ticket.</li></ul><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Kelowna Community Theatre event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF) and 5% GST. A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Opera Kelowna - La Bohème</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
