<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/384601AKTNDSMSHRGBBQBSGDGHKQJPRNV>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "RCA Presents - Birdy by HUNG Dance";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/246f55b9-9083-493c-964d-16a6d1be2d96.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>RCA and Living Things Present </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">BIRDY BY HUNG DANCE</span></h1></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Explore the Digital Program</span><span><br/></span>Get to know the artists and discover more about <span class=\"ItalicText\">Birdy</span> by HUNG Dance. View the show's digital program before or during the performance.<span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://rotarycentreforthearts.com/events/in-the-theatre/birdy-program-2026/\">View the Digital Program</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Birdy</span> blends the flowing movements of Tai chi with contemporary dance, set to electronic and traditional Chinese music. Sensual and visually striking, it draws you into the rhythm, tension and sheer physical beauty of bodies in motion.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">“A polished, visually stunning treat that has sold out at festivals around the world.” - Stir</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Taiwan’s HUNG Dance dancers move together like a flock of birds, balancing, twisting and catching one another in striking feats of strength and control. Long pheasant feathers sweep through the air, extending their movements in unexpected ways.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Created by choreographer LAI Hung-chung, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Birdy</span> moves between dreamlike beauty and charged physical tension, exploring the desire to break free from whatever holds us back.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Winner of the Special Prize for the Preservation of Humanity Heritage from Italy's NO'HMA Theatre, BIRDY has toured internationally and achieved 20 sold-out performances at the Festival Off Avignon.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">“They look, quite simply, super-human.” - Houston Chronicle</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">“Birdy combines dreamy sensibility with astonishing athleticism” - Pancouver</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Presented by Living Things Festival, Inner Fish Performance and Rotary Centre for the Arts.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>For more information on Birdy, <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pAKvESkq4AE\">visit here</a>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span class=\"BoldText\">Adult  $66.71</span>  ($55.65 base price + $2.36 CIF + $8.70 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Student w/ID  $32.90</span>  ($26.25 base price + $2.36 CIF + $4.29 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mary Irwin Theatre at the Rotary Centre for the Arts event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Birdy by Hung Dance</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
