<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/368201ALJRBKJDJTNGTJVQLLJTPGNMBLN>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Tinariwen";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/c7b76d6b-d9ee-40d1-895e-84fa7bb06ad8.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>MODO-Live, The Plant & Skin & Bones present...</h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">TINARIWEN</span></h1><h2>with special guests Orbital Ensemble</h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><h2><span class=\"BoldText\">IMPORTANT UPDATE REGARDING THE TINARIWEN CANADIAN TOUR</span></h2>Dear Tinariwen friends and fans,<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We appreciate your patience in waiting for an update regarding the postponed Canadian tour.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>As many of you know, the tour was postponed after a devastating fire at the home of a member of Tinariwen’s team destroyed the passports, visas, and other essential travel documents belonging to several members of the touring party. What was already an incredibly difficult situation has continued to take time to resolve, and unfortunately, we are not yet in a position to announce new Canadian tour dates.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We know how disappointing this is — particularly for those of you who made plans, travelled, arranged time off, and were looking forward to seeing this legendary artist perform. What we can say is that we continue to work with band and their team toward rescheduling this tour as soon as possible. We must also allow them time to process and deal with this extremely unfortunate event.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>If you are able to hold onto your ticket, we would be incredibly grateful for your patience and support. Your ticket will remain valid for the rescheduled performance in your city, once the new dates are confirmed. Your continued support means a great deal — especially at a moment when circumstances entirely beyond anyones control have made an already challenging situation even more difficult.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>At the same time, we completely understand that circumstances change. If you are unable to wait for the rescheduled dates, refunds will be available upon request.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We are hopeful that we will be able to share new dates with you soon. Until then, thank you for your extraordinary patience, understanding, and support of Tinariwen and MODO LIVE. We hope you’ll stay with us and that, when the time finally comes, we can welcome you to what will undoubtedly be a very special return to Canada.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>With gratitude,<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Modo Live & Tinariwen<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tinariwen – Hoggar <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>10 albums and over 45 years into their storied career, Tuareg musical pioneers and Grammy-winners Tinariwen are returning to their roots. Fierce advocates for their people’s nomadic culture that exists in the desert borderlands between Mali and Algeria, Tinariwen’s bluesy, guitar-driven music has found global acclaim over the past two decades for its lively blend of Tamasheq-language politicism, syncopated rhythms and soaring melody. On Hoggar, their tenth album, they now stake their claim as elders of this Tuareg musical tradition, going back to their early years of songwriting with acoustic guitars and communal singing around the desert campfire, while also passing the torch onto a younger generation of featured musicians who can continue to keep the flame of rebellion and defiance alive. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Typically choosing to record their albums among the arid flatness of the Central Saharan desert and tuning into the sounds of nature as they find their melodies, recent years and the political unrest in Mali have seen the band forced to find new locations for their creativity. Founding members of the band have relocated to Algeria and when it came to making their tenth record, they found a new home in a studio set up by younger Tuareg band Imarhan in the southern city of Tamanrasset. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 1  $74.24</span>  ($62.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $9.38 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 2  $69.06</span>  ($58.00 base price + $2.36 CIF + $8.70 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 3  $62.74</span>  ($52.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $7.88 service charge)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tier 4  $51.24</span>  ($42.50 base price + $2.36 CIF + $6.38 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices are in CAD and include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Kelowna Community Theatre event tickets include a $2.25 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF) and 5% GST. A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Tinariwen</span> tickets and their applicable service fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
